  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Donor invites a primary attorney named on their LPA
    Given I am signed in as the donor
    When I invite the first primary attorney named on my LPA
    Then a pending invitation should be created for that attorney
    And I should be given a unique invite code to share with them
    And the invitation should carry the attorney's details as captured from my LPA
    And the attorney-invited event should appear in my audit log

  # Why: The donor's management surface — see who has been invited and the state of each relationship
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Donor views the attorneys they have invited
    Given I am signed in as the donor
    And I have invited a primary attorney who has not yet claimed their invite
    When I view my attorneys
    Then I should see that attorney listed as pending alongside their invite code

  # Why: THE activation path — attorney whose identity matches the LPA-extracted details claims the invite and is granted access
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A matching attorney claims an invite and is activated
    Given I am signed in as an attorney whose name and date of birth match a primary attorney on the donor's LPA
    And the donor has invited me with an invite code
    When I submit that invite code
    Then my relationship with the donor should become active
    And the donor should appear among the donors I oversee
    And the attorney-activated event should appear in the donor's audit log

  # Why: The attorney's dashboard — the list of donors they may oversee, with a financial summary per donor
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: An activated attorney lists the donors they oversee
    Given I am signed in as an attorney with an active relationship to a donor
